{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557430-extinct-fera-how-and-why","id":1557430,"title":"Extinct Fera: How and Why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-09T18:15:20-08:00","id":1557430,"title":"Extinct Fera: How and Why?","content":"So, from what I've been told in regards to 5th edition, being a Garou, or any type of shifter, is no longer something that is linked to your bloodline, or cultural background. Anybody at any point can undergo the First Change and become a servant of Gaia. Seemingly at complete random, with no real discernible cause as to what made them worthy in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> This got me to thinking. If becoming one of the Changing Breeds is now just a spontaneous event that can strike at any moment, then how is it that some of the tribes / changing breeds were 'hunted to extinction' over the ages? Because the way I see it, there's nothing stopping Gaia (or whoever is responsible) from just spontaneously creating new members to replenish their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T18:54:58-08:00","id":1557433,"title":"","content":"That's because the W5 authors copy pasted the lore of previous edition without adapting it to their new metaphysics. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T20:33:58-08:00","id":1557439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557430-extinct-fera-how-and-why#post1557430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This got me to thinking. If becoming one of the Changing Breeds is now just a spontaneous event that can strike at any moment, then how is it that some of the tribes / changing breeds were 'hunted to extinction' over the ages? Because the way I see it, there's nothing stopping Gaia (or whoever is responsible) from just spontaneously creating new members to replenish their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides a whole lot of sloppiness in W5's setting construction...<br /> <br /> 1) We don't really know what the deal with the non-Garou shifters are in W5. We know they exist on some level, but the books have been avoiding them being so directly parallel to the Garou.<br /> <br /> 2) The game doesn't paint this is purely spontaneous. The presence and desires of Patron spirits still matters. The Patrons of shifters or Tribes could give up on making new followers and thus no more would crop up. The complete destruction of a Patron spirit could also mean the death of a given group within a generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":""